# Programs in the FUZIX test corpus that are NOT identical to their
# .expected files when run with a display (tests/sweep/run-corpus.sh).
# Five are the files' own limitation: the .expected was blessed on a
# host with no display, no sound and no /dev/sys, and with a server
# the program reads something real - mminfo's lock state, printat's
# cursor escapes, the one legitimate PLAY SOUND in play and strargs
# (the goldens expect "Sound output did not start" and it plays), and
# webservz's MM.INFO(IP ADDRESS) (the golden says 0.0.0.0 and the
# server answers with the machine's address).  Ten are the pin and
# peripheral tests, which a PC refuses until phase 8.  A name leaving
# this list is progress; a name arriving is a fault.
mminfo
printat
play
strargs
webservz
countpin
gpio
i2c2
pinint
pioout
port
pulse
pulsin
pwm
waitint
